// machine.fm: forced induction as a machine in the gas path (boost.model = 1): turbochargers and superchargers, the
// charge path they fill and the exhaust that drives them, solved every sample.
//
// The charge path is a chain of volumes that hold mass and energy (gas.fm's BoostVolume), filled and emptied every
// sample: the air outside, through the filter's loss (quasi-steady: 2.5 kPa at the engine's full flow) into the
// compressor (compressor.fm: its map, and the air in its duct, which is what surges); the charge pipe (v1) with the
// blow-off valve's tap; the intercooler, a duct whose air has inertia and whose loss grows with the flow squared
// (its rated drop at its rated flow), an effectiveness against a core that warms (a thermal mass of aluminium, 900
// J/kg K, cooled by the air through it: 200 W/K standing, 30 more each m/s); and the volume before the throttle
// (v2), whose pressure and temperature the intake reads where the reference read pBox and tAir, and from which the
// intake draws (draw()). Volumes are stepped first and the inertial flows after, each sample (symplectic Euler): the
// pipes' and the cooler's Helmholtz oscillations neither grow nor die by the integration.
//
// The exhaust side is the turbine's housing (turbine.fm), a volume the exhaust's pipes end in: the exhaust gives it
// each sample the pipes' drive and admittance and it gives back its pressure (housing()); the nozzle and an internal
// gate empty it into the downpipe, solved against that pipe's end (downpipe()); an external gate into a pipe of its
// own (gatePipe()). The shaft (shaft.fm) takes the turbine's power less the compressor's and the bearings'.
//
// Control (every 16 samples): the wastegate's actuator is a spring that opens the gate as the boost passes its
// rating (fully 10 kPa over it: a stiff actuator; judgement) and a little more with the exhaust's push on its poppet
// (3 % of the pressure before the turbine above the outside; judgement), and a duty that bleeds its signal (a PI
// loop here on the boost before the throttle, to the ECU's target or the spec's) so the gate stays shut longer. A
// variable nozzle's vanes take the loop's output instead. The blow-off valve opens on the pressure across the
// throttle against its spring (fully 10 kPa over it, in 3 ms). A sequential pair's second turbo joins above an
// engine flow (its exhaust transfer valve and its compressor's outlet open together in 0.15 s; below 80 % of it they
// close). Over-speed, over-boost, surge and choke are flagged.
//
// Arrangements (layout): one; two side by side, a bank each, into one charge pipe; sequential (turbo 0 alone below
// the flow, turbo 1 joining); compound (turbo 1 the big low-pressure stage, its compressor first and its turbine
// last; turbo 0 the small high-pressure one, fed by an interstage volume and emptying into turbo 1's housing); four,
// two a bank. Superchargers (kind 4): Roots and twin-screw (supercharger.fm) or a centrifugal (this file's
// compressor on a gear, comp[0], its speed the crank's times the pulley's and the step-up's); a bypass round it at
// part throttle; the crank's torque from its work over its efficiency (0.9 for the positive-displacement ones, 0.95
// for the centrifugal's gear).
//
// Anti-lag (the ECU decides when, card H): the fuel it sends past the engine burns in turbo 0's housing in events at
// random (some 3 ms apart while the housing is above 750 K and the shaft under its limit, each its pool's heat over
// half a millisecond, at 70 % of the fuel's 43 MJ/kg): the wheel keeps its speed off the throttle, and each event is a bang. Nitrous (the ECU opens
// its window): a mass flow by the shot's size (the rating over 2.13 MJ a kilogram: its oxygen's share, 0.364, burning
// gasoline at 3.41 kg of oxygen a kilogram and 43 MJ/kg, with its decomposition's 1.86 MJ/kg, at a brake
// efficiency of 0.33), from a bottle whose pressure falls to 65 % as it empties; into v2, its oxygen raising the
// charge's oxygen share (oxygen(): 0.232 for air), its evaporation (300 kJ/kg: judgement, between N2O's latent heat
// at 20 C and at its boiling point) cooling the charge. A purge vents it, as a sound.
//
// Sizes left at 0 are matched to the engine (match()): the flow the engine takes at its redline at a pressure ratio
// of 1.9 and 90 % volumetric efficiency, shared among the turbos; the compressor chokes 15 % above it; the turbine's
// nozzle passes 65 % of it at 2.4 bar and 1150 K, choked; the times the spec's size. The gate, whatever the size,
// passes the whole of the turbo's share alone at that state (a gate sized at 0.85 of the nozzle could not hold its
// spring at the redline: the 2 L four spooled at 5300 rpm ran away to 2.6 bar with it wide open; card N2's
// docs/measurements/calibration/boost/gate.md). A 2 L four at 7000 rpm gets a 45 mm inducer, a 61 mm exducer (a
// GT28's class) and a 35 mm gate. `vd` is the four-stroke-equivalent displacement: the volume whose four-stroke air
// at redRpm is the engine's (Engine passes a rotary's and a two-stroke's swept volume twice: 2df7ea6, d9c5544). A
// sequential pair's first gate passes the whole engine's flow (every collector ends in its housing).
//
// Left out: the turbine's housing walls' heat; heat between the turbine and the compressor; the compressor inlet's
// swirl and recirculation; the gate's flutter; the intercooler's own volume's Helmholtz (folded into v2); a second
// intercooler between a compound pair's stages; anti-lag's misfires in the cylinders (card H).
//
// The order of a sample (the exhaust's and the intake's calls are theirs; what this file asks of them):
//   housing(h, drive, admit, tGas)   the exhaust, for each housing its pipes end in, before it writes them
//   downpipe(s, a, z), gatePipe(t, a, z)   the exhaust, for each downpipe and external gate's pipe
//   pressure(), temperature()        the intake, for the throttle (the state at the start of this sample)
//   draw(m)                          the intake: what the throttle took this sample, kg/s
//   tick(omegaCrank, pPlenum)        then this: the charge path, the shafts, the sounds
//   control(d16)                     every 16 samples
#pragma once
#include "gas.fm"
#include "compressor.fm"
#include "turbine.fm"
#include "shaft.fm"
#include "supercharger.fm"
#include "sound.fm"
#include "spec/boost.fm"

enum
{
    BOOST_ONE = 1,
    BOOST_TWIN = 2,
    BOOST_SEQUENTIAL = 3,
    BOOST_COMPOUND = 4,
    BOOST_QUAD = 5
};

enum
{
    BOOST_FLAG_SURGE = 1,
    BOOST_FLAG_CHOKE = 2,
    BOOST_FLAG_OVERSPEED = 4,
    BOOST_FLAG_OVERBOOST = 8,
    BOOST_FLAG_BLOWOFF = 16,
    BOOST_FLAG_NITROUS = 32
};

module BoostMachine
{
    float rate;
    float dt;
    float pOut;         // the air outside: Pa absolute, K
    float tOut;
    float vd;           // the engine's displacement, m^3, and its redline, rpm (for matched sizes)
    float redRpm;
    int active;         // the charge path runs: a turbo, a supercharger, or nitrous
    int kind;           // 0 natural, 1 to 3 turbos, 4 a supercharger
    int turbos;         // shafts in use (a centrifugal supercharger: comp[0], no turbine)
    int layout;
    int sc;             // 0 none, 1 Roots, 2 twin-screw, 3 centrifugal
    int scrolls;
    int structure;      // what apply() last built (a change of it rebuilds at rest)
    BoostCompressor comp[BOOST_TURBOS];
    BoostTurbine turb[BOOST_TURBOS];
    BoostShaft shaft[BOOST_TURBOS];
    BoostHousing house[BOOST_HOUSINGS];
    BoostEnd end;
    BoostSupercharger pd;
    BoostVolume vInter;     // between a compound pair's stages
    BoostVolume vSec;       // a sequential pair's second compressor's outlet
    BoostVolume v1;         // the charge pipe, compressor to intercooler
    BoostVolume v2;         // intercooler to throttle: what the intake draws from
    BoostSound snd;
    int compIn[BOOST_TURBOS];       // 0: the air outside; 1: vInter
    int compOut[BOOST_TURBOS];      // 0: v1; 1: vInter; 2: vSec
    int turbOut[BOOST_TURBOS];      // -1: a downpipe (turbSide); a housing's index otherwise
    int turbSide[BOOST_TURBOS];
    int exSides;        // the exhaust's sides (card G tells, at every configure; 2 until it does): a turbo of side 1 on a
                        // one-sided exhaust empties into side 0's downpipe
    float omegaMax[BOOST_TURBOS];
    float mMatch;                   // the engine's flow at its redline, matched, kg/s
    // (card N2: the charge system against the engine it is on, for the telemetry's warnings: has, wants; see apply)
    float icFlowHas;
    float chargeVolHas;
    float compFlowHas;              // the compressors' choke flows in standard air, summed where they draw from the air
    // the inlet
    float kFilter;
    float mInlet;       // through the filter (negative: out of it), kg/s
    float p1;
    float t1;
    float mBack;        // hot air sent back out of the inlet (surge, a recirculating valve, leaks), kg/s, and its K
    float tBack;
    // the intercooler
    float icK;
    float icDuct;
    float mIc;
    float mNa;          // a natural engine's (nitrous only): the inlet's duct straight into v1
    float icEff;
    float tCore;
    float qCore;        // the heat into the core over the last 16 samples, J (integrated at the control rate: a
                        // sample's warming is under a float's step at 300 K)
    float cCore;
    float gCool;
    float tIcOut;
    float airSpeed;     // the air through the car's front, m/s
    int cellHeld;       // 1: an engine test cell's charge-air cooling holds the core at the air's temperature
    float mIcSlow;      // the cooler's flow (kg/s) and its inlet's temperature (K), followed over 1 s (the settle's)
    float tIcInSlow;
    // the intake's side
    float mDraw;
    float pPlenum;
    float omegaCrank;
    // blow-off
    int bovKind;
    float bovArea;
    float bovSpring;
    float bovLift;
    float bpLimit;      // a variable nozzle's limit on the pressure before the turbine over the boost (absolute)
    float bpOpen[BOOST_TURBOS];  // the limit's opening of the vanes, each turbo
    float surgeOpen[BOOST_TURBOS];  // the surge guard's opening of the vanes, each turbo
    float bovAt;        // the blow-off valve's opening the air sees: bovLift followed every sample by two 1 ms stages
    float bovMid;
    float kAt;          // that following's step a sample
    float mBov;
    // control
    float gateSpring;
    float gateSpan;
    float kFace;
    float target;       // the spec's boost target, Pa (0: the spring)
    float cmdTarget;    // the ECU's (below 0: none given)
    float cmdVanes;     // the ECU's vanes (below 0: the loop's)
    float duty;
    float integ;
    float overBoost;
    float assistCmd;
    // sequential
    float seqOpen;
    float seqWant;
    float seqFlow;
    float aTransfer;
    float aSecValve;
    float drawMean;
    // supercharger
    float scRatio;
    float scStepUp;
    int scBypass;
    float bypassArea;
    float bypassOpen;
    float scDrive;      // W from the crank this sample
    float crankTorque;  // N m the forced induction takes from the crank, over the last 16 samples
    float driveSum;
    // nitrous
    float nShot;
    float nRated;
    float nBottle;
    float nLeft;
    int cmdNitrous;     // the ECU's window: 1 open
    int cmdPurge;       // counts purges
    int purgeSeen;
    float purge;
    float mNitrous;
    // anti-lag
    int antiLag;
    float cmdAntiLag;   // kg/s of fuel the ECU sends to burn in the housing
    float alPool;
    float alHeat;       // W, released over the event
    int alLeft;
    int alSeed;
    float alKick;
    // the downpipes and external gates' pipes: what goes into them
    float dpMass[BOOST_SIDES];
    float dpTemp[BOOST_SIDES];
    float qSrc[BOOST_HOUSINGS];     // each turbo's flow into its downpipe at the last solve (at 2 t)
    float gateMass[BOOST_TURBOS];
    float gateTemp[BOOST_TURBOS];
    // what the outside reads: every 16 samples (instantaneous unless the name says mean)
    float telSpeed[BOOST_TURBOS];   // rad/s
    float telPr[BOOST_TURBOS];      // the compressor's pressure ratio
    float telFlow[BOOST_TURBOS];    // its corrected flow, kg/s at 101325 Pa and 293.15 K
    float telEta[BOOST_TURBOS];
    float telT2[BOOST_TURBOS];      // its outlet's temperature, K
    float telGate[BOOST_TURBOS];    // the gate's opening, 0 to 1
    float telVanes[BOOST_TURBOS];
    float telPTurb[BOOST_TURBOS];   // before the turbine, Pa absolute (a twin scroll's mean)
    float telTTurb[BOOST_TURBOS];
    float telDrive[BOOST_TURBOS];   // that over the boost's absolute pressure
    float telBoost;                 // before the throttle, Pa above the outside
    float telIcOut;                 // K
    float telScPower;               // W the supercharger takes from the crank
    float telO2;
    int flags;
    // the map, for a view: speed lines (corrected flow and ratio), the surge line, efficiency contours, the trail
    float lineFlow[BOOST_LINES][BOOST_LINEPTS];
    float linePr[BOOST_LINES][BOOST_LINEPTS];
    float lineSpeed[BOOST_LINES];               // rad/s of each line
    float surgeFlow[BOOST_LINES];
    float surgePr[BOOST_LINES];
    float contourFlow[BOOST_LEVELS][BOOST_CONTOUR];   // a contour's points (flow below 0: none there)
    float contourPr[BOOST_LEVELS][BOOST_CONTOUR];
    float contourEta[BOOST_LEVELS];
    float trailFlow[BOOST_TRAIL];
    float trailPr[BOOST_TRAIL];
    int trailAt;
    int trailTick;
    int mapRev;         // counts rebuilds of the map's lines
    // sums for tests and means (seconds of energy and mass)
    double sumPt[BOOST_TURBOS];     // J the turbine gave
    double sumPc[BOOST_TURBOS];     // J the compressor took
    double sumPf[BOOST_TURBOS];     // J the bearings took
    double sumPm[BOOST_TURBOS];     // J the motor gave
    double sumMComp;                // kg through the compressors (first stage)
    double sumMDraw;                // kg the intake drew
    double sumMPipes;               // kg the exhaust's pipes put into the housings
    double sumMDown;                // kg into the downpipes
    double sumMGate;                // kg into external gates' pipes
    double sumMBov;
    double sumScDrive;              // J from the crank
    double sumScAir;                // J of the air's work (the supercharger's)
    double sumMNitrous;
    // the sounds, this sample
    float outInlet;
    float outVent;
    float outCase;
    float outBang;

    void setup(float rateIn, float vdIn, float redIn)
    {
        rate = rateIn;
        dt = 1.0f / rate;
        kAt = 1.0f - expf(-dt / 0.001f);
        exSides = 2;
        pOut = 101325.0f;
        tOut = 293.15f;
        vd = vdIn;
        redRpm = redIn;
        structure = -1;
        kind = 0;
        active = 0;
        turbos = 0;
        cmdTarget = -1.0f;
        cmdVanes = -1.0f;
        v1.setup(0.002f, pOut, tOut, kBoostCpA, kBoostCvA);
        v2.setup(0.003f, pOut, tOut, kBoostCpA, kBoostCvA);
        vInter.setup(0.0015f, pOut, tOut, kBoostCpA, kBoostCvA);
        vSec.setup(0.0008f, pOut, tOut, kBoostCpA, kBoostCvA);
        for (int h = 0; h < BOOST_HOUSINGS; ++h)
            house[h].setup(0.0002f, pOut, tOut);
        snd.setup(rate);
        reset();
    }

    // The air outside (the environment's), Pa absolute and K
    void ambient(float p, float t)
    {
        pOut = p;
        tOut = t;
    }

    // At rest: every volume at the air outside, every flow and shaft stopped
    void reset()
    {
        v1.reset(pOut, tOut);
        v2.reset(pOut, tOut);
        vInter.reset(pOut, tOut);
        vSec.reset(pOut, tOut);
        for (int h = 0; h < BOOST_HOUSINGS; ++h)
        {
            house[h].setup(house[h].vol, pOut, tOut);
            qSrc[h] = 0.0f;
        }
        for (int t = 0; t < BOOST_TURBOS; ++t)
        {
            comp[t].reset(pOut, tOut);
            shaft[t].omega = 0.0f;
            turb[t].begin();
            turb[t].lift = 0.0f;
            turb[t].liftAt = 0.0f;
            turb[t].liftMid = 0.0f;
            turb[t].vanes = 1.0f;
            turb[t].vanesAt = 1.0f;
            turb[t].vanesMid = 1.0f;
            bpOpen[t] = 0.0f;
            surgeOpen[t] = 0.0f;
            gateMass[t] = 0.0f;
            gateTemp[t] = tOut;
        }
        for (int s = 0; s < BOOST_SIDES; ++s)
        {
            dpMass[s] = 0.0f;
            dpTemp[s] = tOut;
        }
        mInlet = 0.0f;
        p1 = pOut;
        t1 = tOut;
        mBack = 0.0f;
        tBack = tOut;
        mIc = 0.0f;
        mNa = 0.0f;
        tCore = tOut;
        cellHeld = 0;
        mIcSlow = 0.0f;
        tIcInSlow = tOut;
        qCore = 0.0f;
        tIcOut = tOut;
        mDraw = 0.0f;
        pPlenum = pOut;
        bovLift = 0.0f;
        bovAt = 0.0f;
        bovMid = 0.0f;
        mBov = 0.0f;
        duty = 0.0f;
        integ = 0.0f;
        seqOpen = 0.0f;
        seqWant = 0.0f;
        drawMean = 0.0f;
        bypassOpen = 1.0f;
        scDrive = 0.0f;
        crankTorque = 0.0f;
        driveSum = 0.0f;
        nLeft = nBottle;
        purge = 0.0f;
        mNitrous = 0.0f;
        alPool = 0.0f;
        alHeat = 0.0f;
        alLeft = 0;
        alKick = 0.0f;
        flags = 0;
        trailAt = 0;
        trailTick = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < BOOST_TRAIL; ++i)
        {
            trailFlow[i] = 0.0f;
            trailPr[i] = 1.0f;
        }
        snd.clear();
        outInlet = 0.0f;
        outVent = 0.0f;
        outCase = 0.0f;
        outBang = 0.0f;
        telBoost = 0.0f;
        telIcOut = tOut;
        telO2 = 0.232f;
    }

    // The spec's section, read when its rev moves. A change of what the machine is (the kind, the arrangement, the
    // scrolls, the supercharger) rebuilds it at rest; the rest is taken as it comes.
    void apply(BoostSpec* s)
    {
        kind = s->kind;
        int lay = s->layout;
        if (kind >= 1 && kind <= 3)
        {
            if (lay == 0)
                lay = kind == 1 ? BOOST_ONE : (kind == 2 ? BOOST_TWIN : BOOST_QUAD);
        }
        else
            lay = 0;
        layout = lay;
        sc = kind == 4 ? 1 + s->charger : 0;
        scrolls = sc == 0 && kind != 0 ? s->scrolls : 1;
        turbos = layout == BOOST_ONE ? 1 : (layout == BOOST_QUAD ? 4 : (layout == 0 ? 0 : 2));
        if (sc == 3)
            turbos = 1;
        nShot = s->nitrousShot;
        active = kind != 0 || nShot > 0.0f ? 1 : 0;
        const int st = kind + 8 * layout + 64 * scrolls + 256 * sc + 2048 * active;
        // the topology
        for (int t = 0; t < BOOST_TURBOS; ++t)
        {
            compIn[t] = 0;
            compOut[t] = 0;
            turbOut[t] = -1;
            turbSide[t] = 0;
        }
        if (layout == BOOST_TWIN)
            turbSide[1] = 1;
        if (layout == BOOST_QUAD)
        {
            turbSide[2] = 1;
            turbSide[3] = 1;
        }
        if (layout == BOOST_SEQUENTIAL)
            compOut[1] = 2;
        if (layout == BOOST_COMPOUND)
        {
            compIn[0] = 1;
            compOut[1] = 1;
            turbOut[0] = 2;      // turbo 1's (first) housing
        }
        // sizes: matched to the engine where left at 0
        mMatch = fmaxf(vd * redRpm / 120.0f * 1.204f * 1.9f * 0.9f, 0.01f);
        const float share = layout == BOOST_TWIN ? 0.5f : (layout == BOOST_QUAD ? 0.25f : (layout == BOOST_SEQUENTIAL ? 0.55f : 1.0f));
        for (int t = 0; t < BOOST_TURBOS; ++t)
        {
            // (a compound pair's high-pressure stage meets air already compressed some 1.6 times: a smaller wheel)
            const float mt = mMatch * share * s->size * (layout == BOOST_COMPOUND && t == 0 ? 0.65f : 1.0f);
            const float wide = expf(0.25f * logf(fmaxf(s->compAR, 0.2f) / 0.6f));
            const float aAnn = 1.15f * mt / (0.45f * 1.204f * 343.2f * wide);
            float dInd = s->compInducer > 0.0f ? s->compInducer : 2.0f * sqrtf(aAnn / (0.91f * 3.14159265f));
            float dEx = s->compExducer > 0.0f ? s->compExducer : dInd / 0.7416f;
            if (sc == 3 && s->compExducer <= 0.0f)
            {
                // a centrifugal supercharger's wheel: about 300 m/s at the tip at the redline
                const float wRed = redRpm * 0.10471976f * s->scRatio * s->scStepUp;
                dEx = fmaxf(dInd / 0.8f, 600.0f / fmaxf(wRed, 100.0f));
            }
            comp[t].size(dInd, dEx, s->compAR, s->compEta, dt);
            // (the warnings' compressor: its choke flow, std air, as aAnn's rule reads it backward: 0.45 rho a A wide)
            if (t == 0)
                compFlowHas = 0.0f;
            if (t < turbos && !(layout == BOOST_COMPOUND && t == 0))
                compFlowHas += 0.45f * 1.204f * 343.2f * wide * 0.91f * 3.14159265f * 0.25f * dInd * dInd;
            const float dT = s->turbWheel > 0.0f ? s->turbWheel : 0.9f * dEx;
            const float rc = 0.6f * dT;
            float aNoz = 0.0f;
            if (s->turbAR > 0.0f)
                aNoz = s->turbAR * 0.0254f * rc;
            else
                aNoz = 0.65f * mt * sqrtf(kBoostR * 1150.0f) / (2.4e5f * 0.667f);
            turb[t].rWheel = 0.5f * dT;
            turb[t].aNoz = aNoz;
            turb[t].etaMax = s->turbEta;
            turb[t].vgt = s->vanes;
            turb[t].vaneMin = s->vaneMin;
            bpLimit = s->backPressure;
            turb[t].gateExt = s->gate;
            turb[t].scrolls = scrolls;
            // the gate, matched: open, it alone passes this turbo's whole share of the engine's matched flow at the
            // nozzle's design state (2.4 bar, 1150 K, choked), whatever the turbo's size: a wastegate must bypass
            // nearly all the exhaust when the turbine at full flow could make several times the compressor's need
            // (Bell, Maximum Boost, ch. 6; Watson and Janota, ch. 9). 0.85 is the poppet's discharge coefficient.
            // (a sequential pair's first housing takes every collector, the second turbine fed from it only through the
            // transfer valve: its gate bypasses the whole engine's flow)
            const float mGate = mMatch * (layout == BOOST_SEQUENTIAL && t == 0 ? 1.0f : share)
                                * (layout == BOOST_COMPOUND && t == 0 ? 0.65f : 1.0f);
            const float aGateMatched = mGate * sqrtf(kBoostR * 1150.0f) / (2.4e5f * 0.667f);
            const float dg = s->gateDiameter > 0.0f ? s->gateDiameter : sqrtf(aGateMatched / (0.785398f * 0.85f));
            turb[t].aGate = 0.785398f * dg * dg * 0.85f;
            const float vh = s->housingVolume > 0.0f ? s->housingVolume : 4.0f * 3.14159265f * rc * aNoz;
            for (int k = 0; k < 2; ++k)
                house[2 * t + k].resize(vh / (float)scrolls);
            shaft[t].size(s->inertia, dT, dEx, s->bearing, s->assist);
            omegaMax[t] = s->maxSpeed > 0.0f ? s->maxSpeed : 560.0f / comp[t].rTip;
        }
        aTransfer = turb[1].aNoz;
        aSecValve = comp[1].aInd * 1.5f;
        seqFlow = s->seqFlow > 0.0f ? s->seqFlow : 0.4f * mMatch;
        // the charge path
        kFilter = 2500.0f / (mMatch * mMatch);
        v1.resize(0.4f * s->chargeVolume);
        v2.resize(0.6f * s->chargeVolume);
        icEff = s->icEffect;
        icK = s->icDrop / (s->icFlow * s->icFlow);
        icFlowHas = s->icFlow;
        chargeVolHas = s->chargeVolume;
        icDuct = dt * 0.008f / 0.8f;
        cCore = s->icMass * 900.0f;
        bovKind = s->blowOffKind;
        bovArea = 0.785398f * s->blowOffDiameter * s->blowOffDiameter * 0.8f;
        bovSpring = s->blowOffSpring;
        gateSpring = s->gateSpring;
        gateSpan = 10000.0f;
        kFace = 0.03f;
        target = s->target;
        overBoost = s->overBoost > 0.0f ? s->overBoost : 1.4f * fmaxf(target, gateSpring);
        // superchargers
        scRatio = s->scRatio;
        scStepUp = s->scStepUp;
        scBypass = s->scBypass ? 1 : 0;
        const float disp = s->scDisplacement > 0.0f ? s->scDisplacement : 0.27f * vd * s->size;
        pd.size(disp, sc == 2 ? s->scVolumeRatio : 1.0f);
        bypassArea = 0.785398f * 0.045f * 0.045f * expf(0.5f * logf(fmaxf(vd / 0.003f, 0.1f)));
        // extras
        antiLag = s->antiLag ? 1 : 0;
        nRated = nShot / 2.13e6f;
        nBottle = s->nitrousBottle;
        if (st != structure)
        {
            structure = st;
            reset();
        }
        mapLines();
    }

    // ---- the exhaust's side ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    // Which housing a collector feeds: the bank it is on (0, 1), which group of cylinders it gathers (0, 1: a twin
    // scroll's or a second turbo's on that bank), and how many banks the engine has. -1: no turbine (its pipe goes on
    // as the reference's does).
    int housingOf(int bank, int group, int banks)
    {
        if (active == 0 || turbos == 0 || sc != 0)
            return -1;
        // (twin turbos: a bank each; on one bank, its collectors in order, the front's to turbo 0 and the rear's to
        // turbo 1, a straight six's 1-3 and 4-6: so each wheel has its gas, card N2's)
        if (layout == BOOST_TWIN)
            return banks > 1 ? 2 * (bank & 1) + (scrolls == 2 ? (group & 1) : 0) : 2 * (group & 1);
        if (layout == BOOST_QUAD)
            return 2 * (2 * (bank & 1) + (group & 1));
        // one wheel takes every collector (a sequential pair's first, a compound pair's high-pressure stage)
        if (scrolls == 2)
            return banks > 1 ? (bank & 1) : (group & 1);
        return 0;
    }

    // The downpipe (exhaust side) turbo t empties into: its own, or side 0's when the exhaust has one side
    int sideOf(int t)
    {
        return turbSide[t] < exSides ? turbSide[t] : 0;
    }

    // One sample, for each housing the exhaust's pipes end in, before it writes them: the pipes' drive (sum of
    // 2 a_i / z_i, m^3/s) and admittance (sum of 1 / z_i) and their gas's temperature (K). Returns the housing's
    // pressure above the outside (Pa): each pipe then sends back b_i = p - a_i.
    float housing(int h, float drive, float admit, float tGas) [[clang::nonblocking]]
    {
        if (active == 0 || h < 0 || h >= 2 * turbos)
            return 0.0f;
        const float pg = house[h].solve(drive, admit, tGas, pOut, dt);
        sumMPipes += (double)(house[h].qPipes * house[h].p / (kBoostR * (house[h].qPipes >= 0.0f ? tGas : house[h].t)) * dt);
        return pg;
    }

    // One sample, for downpipe s (one a bank): the wave arriving at its near end (Pa) and its impedance. Solves every
    // nozzle and internal gate that empties into it against that end at once; returns the end's pressure above the
    // outside (the pipe sends back p - a). dpMass[s] and dpTemp[s] are then what went in.
    //
    // Each turbo is one source against the pipe (BoostEnd: exact for one); several turbos on one pipe by two
    // Gauss-Seidel sweeps, each against the pipe with the others' flows of the sweep before. A twin scroll's two
    // housings are one source at their mean state for that solve; the flow is then shared between them by each one's
    // own orifice law at the end's pressure, the difference from the solve's total spread by their areas, so what
    // leaves the housings is what the pipe takes (one solve and two orifices, not four solves).
    float downpipe(int s, float a, float z) [[clang::nonblocking]]
    {
        const float pq = pOut + 2.0f * a;
        if (active == 0 || turbos == 0 || sc != 0)
        {
            dpMass[s] = 0.0f;
            return 0.0f;
        }
        float qSum = 0.0f;
        int sources = 0;
        for (int t = 0; t < turbos; ++t)
            if (turbOut[t] < 0 && sideOf(t) == s)
            {
                qSum += qSrc[2 * t];
                sources += 1;
            }
        if (sources == 0)
        {
            dpMass[s] = 0.0f;
            return 0.0f;
        }
        const int sweeps = sources > 1 ? 2 : 1;
        for (int sweep = 0; sweep < sweeps; ++sweep)
            for (int t = 0; t < turbos; ++t)
            {
                if (turbOut[t] >= 0 || sideOf(t) != s)
                    continue;
                const int h = 2 * t;
                const float area = turb[t].nozzle() + (turb[t].gateExt == 0 ? turb[t].aGate * turb[t].liftAt : 0.0f);
                float pc = house[h].p;
                float tc = house[h].t;
                float vh = house[h].vol;
                if (scrolls == 2)
                {
                    pc = 0.5f * (house[h].p + house[h + 1].p);
                    tc = 0.5f * (house[h].t + house[h + 1].t);
                    vh += house[h + 1].vol;
                }
                const float zc = dt * (4.0f / 3.0f) * pc / vh;
                const float q = end.flow(pc, tc, pq + z * (qSum - qSrc[h]), z, area, dpTemp[s], zc);
                qSum += q - qSrc[h];
                qSrc[h] = q;
            }
        const float pp = pq + z * qSum;
        float mSum = 0.0f;
        float hSum = 0.0f;
        for (int t = 0; t < turbos; ++t)
        {
            if (turbOut[t] >= 0 || sideOf(t) != s)
                continue;
            const int h0 = 2 * t;
            const float an = turb[t].nozzle() / (float)scrolls;
            const float area = an + (turb[t].gateExt == 0 ? turb[t].aGate * turb[t].liftAt / (float)scrolls : 0.0f);
            const float q = qSrc[h0];
            const float tc = scrolls == 2 ? 0.5f * (house[h0].t + house[h0 + 1].t) : house[h0].t;
            const float mt = q * pp / (kBoostR * (q >= 0.0f ? tc : dpTemp[s]));
            float ms[2];
            ms[0] = mt;
            ms[1] = 0.0f;
            if (scrolls == 2)
            {
                ms[0] = boostOrificeStep(house[h0].p, house[h0].t, pp, dpTemp[s], area, 1, boostStiff(house[h0].vol, house[h0].t, 1.3333333f, dt));
                ms[1] = boostOrificeStep(house[h0 + 1].p, house[h0 + 1].t, pp, dpTemp[s], area, 1, boostStiff(house[h0 + 1].vol, house[h0 + 1].t, 1.3333333f, dt));
                const float rest = 0.5f * (mt - ms[0] - ms[1]);
                ms[0] += rest;
                ms[1] += rest;
            }
            for (int k = 0; k < scrolls; ++k)
            {
                const int h = h0 + k;
                const float m = ms[k];
                house[h].mOutPipe = m;
                if (m >= 0.0f)
                {
                    const float mn = area > 1.0e-10f ? m * an / area : 0.0f;
                    const float w = turb[t].work(mn, house[h].t, pp / house[h].p, shaft[t].omega);
                    turb[t].mNoz += mn;
                    turb[t].mGate += m - mn;
                    mSum += m;
                    hSum += m * kBoostCpE * house[h].t - w;
                }
                else
                {
                    mSum += m;
                    hSum += m * kBoostCpE * dpTemp[s];
                }
            }
        }
        dpMass[s] = mSum;
        if (mSum > 1.0e-6f)
            dpTemp[s] = fminf(fmaxf(hSum / (mSum * kBoostCpE), 250.0f), 2500.0f);
        sumMDown += (double)(mSum * dt);
        return pp - pOut;
    }

    // One sample, for turbo t's external gate: the wave arriving at its pipe's near end and its impedance. Returns the
    // end's pressure above the outside; gateMass[t] and gateTemp[t] are what went in.
    float gatePipe(int t, float a, float z) [[clang::nonblocking]]
    {
        if (active == 0 || t >= turbos || turb[t].gateExt == 0 || sc != 0)
        {
            gateMass[t] = 0.0f;
            return 0.0f;
        }
        const float pq = pOut + 2.0f * a;
        const float area = turb[t].aGate * turb[t].liftAt;
        const int h0 = 2 * t;
        float pc = house[h0].p;
        float tc = house[h0].t;
        float vh = house[h0].vol;
        if (scrolls == 2)
        {
            pc = 0.5f * (house[h0].p + house[h0 + 1].p);
            tc = 0.5f * (house[h0].t + house[h0 + 1].t);
            vh += house[h0 + 1].vol;
        }
        const float q = end.flow(pc, tc, pq, z, area, tOut, dt * (4.0f / 3.0f) * pc / vh);
        const float pp = pq + z * q;
        const float tg = q >= 0.0f ? tc : tOut;
        const float mt = q * pp / (kBoostR * tg);
        float ms[2];
        ms[0] = mt;
        ms[1] = 0.0f;
        if (scrolls == 2)
        {
            ms[0] = boostOrificeStep(house[h0].p, house[h0].t, pp, tOut, 0.5f * area, 1, boostStiff(house[h0].vol, house[h0].t, 1.3333333f, dt));
            ms[1] = boostOrificeStep(house[h0 + 1].p, house[h0 + 1].t, pp, tOut, 0.5f * area, 1, boostStiff(house[h0 + 1].vol, house[h0 + 1].t, 1.3333333f, dt));
            const float rest = 0.5f * (mt - ms[0] - ms[1]);
            ms[0] += rest;
            ms[1] += rest;
        }
        for (int k = 0; k < scrolls; ++k)
            house[h0 + k].mOutGate = ms[k];
        gateMass[t] = mt;
        if (mt > 1.0e-6f)
            gateTemp[t] = tg;
        turb[t].mGate += mt;
        sumMGate += (double)(mt * dt);
        return pp - pOut;
    }

    // ---- the intake's side ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    // The pressure (Pa absolute) and temperature (K) before the throttle; the air outside's when there is nothing
    float pressure()
    {
        return active != 0 ? v2.p : pOut;
    }

    float temperature()
    {
        return active != 0 ? v2.t : tOut;
    }

    // The oxygen's share of the charge's mass (Combustion's: 0.232 for air)
    float oxygen()
    {
        return active != 0 ? v2.o2 : 0.232f;
    }

    // What the throttle took from before it this sample, kg/s (negative: pushed back)
    void draw(float m)
    {
        mDraw = m;
    }

    // ---- one sample -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    void tick(float omegaCrankIn, float pPlenumIn) [[clang::nonblocking]]
    {
        omegaCrank = omegaCrankIn;
        pPlenum = pPlenumIn;
        if (active == 0)
        {
            outInlet = 0.0f;
            outVent = 0.0f;
            outCase = 0.0f;
            outBang = 0.0f;
            crankTorque = 0.0f;
            return;
        }
        // the valves' and the vanes' openings as the gas sees them: the actuators' (moved every 16 samples, and snapped
        // shut or open by the relief) followed every sample by two 1 ms stages, so neither the flow through them nor its
        // rate of change steps (a step is a click; the inlet's sound is the flow's rate of change)
        for (int t = 0; t < turbos; ++t)
        {
            turb[t].liftMid += (turb[t].lift - turb[t].liftMid) * kAt;
            turb[t].liftAt += (turb[t].liftMid - turb[t].liftAt) * kAt;
            turb[t].vanesMid += (turb[t].vanes - turb[t].vanesMid) * kAt;
            turb[t].vanesAt += (turb[t].vanesMid - turb[t].vanesAt) * kAt;
        }
        bovMid += (bovLift - bovMid) * kAt;
        bovAt += (bovMid - bovAt) * kAt;
        exhaustSide();
        chargeSide();
        // the shafts
        for (int t = 0; t < turbos; ++t)
        {
            if (sc == 3)
            {
                shaft[t].omega = omegaCrank * scRatio * scStepUp;
                scDrive = comp[t].power / 0.95f;
            }
            else
            {
                shaft[t].step(turb[t].torque, comp[t].power, assistCmd, dt);
                sumPt[t] += (double)(turb[t].power * dt);
                sumPf[t] += (double)(shaft[t].friction * dt);
                sumPm[t] += (double)(shaft[t].motor * dt);
            }
            sumPc[t] += (double)(comp[t].power * dt);
            turb[t].begin();
        }
        driveSum += scDrive;
        sumScDrive += (double)(scDrive * dt);
        sounds();
    }

    // The exhaust's volumes that no pipe of the exhaust's ends in (stepped here), and the flows between the model's
    // own volumes, for the next sample's solves
    void exhaustSide()
    {
        const int nh = sc == 0 ? 2 * turbos : 0;
        for (int h = 0; h < nh; h += 3 - scrolls)
        {
            if (house[h].stepped == 0)
                house[h].solve(0.0f, 0.0f, tOut, pOut, dt);
            house[h].stepped = 0;
            house[h].mIn = 0.0f;
            house[h].hIn = 0.0f;
            house[h].mOutInt = 0.0f;
            house[h].heatIn = 0.0f;
        }
        if (layout == BOOST_COMPOUND || layout == BOOST_SEQUENTIAL)
        {
            // compound: the high-pressure turbine (0) and its gate empty into the low-pressure one's housing; sequential:
            // the transfer valve from the first housing to the second's
            const int lp = 2;
            for (int k = 0; k < scrolls; ++k)
            {
                const int h = k;
                const int hd = lp + k;
                float an = 0.0f;
                float area = 0.0f;
                if (layout == BOOST_COMPOUND)
                {
                    an = turb[0].nozzle() / (float)scrolls;
                    area = an + turb[0].aGate * turb[0].liftAt / (float)scrolls;
                }
                else
                    area = aTransfer * seqOpen / (float)scrolls;
                const float kk = boostStiff(house[h].vol, house[h].t, 1.3333333f, dt) + boostStiff(house[hd].vol, house[hd].t, 1.3333333f, dt);
                const float m = boostOrificeStep(house[h].p, house[h].t, house[hd].p, house[hd].t, area, 1, kk);
                if (m >= 0.0f)
                {
                    const float mn = area > 1.0e-10f ? m * an / area : 0.0f;
                    const float w = an > 0.0f ? turb[0].work(mn, house[h].t, house[hd].p / house[h].p, shaft[0].omega) : 0.0f;
                    turb[0].mNoz += mn;
                    house[h].mOutInt += m;
                    house[hd].mIn += m;
                    house[hd].hIn += m * kBoostCpE * house[h].t - w;
                }
                else
                {
                    house[hd].mOutInt -= m;
                    house[h].mIn -= m;
                    house[h].hIn -= m * kBoostCpE * house[hd].t;
                }
            }
        }
        // anti-lag: the fuel sent past the engine pools in turbo 0's housing and lights at random when it is hot
        alKick = 0.0f;
        if (antiLag != 0 && turbos > 0 && sc == 0)
        {
            alPool = fminf(alPool + cmdAntiLag * dt, 2.0e-4f);
            if (alLeft > 0)
            {
                house[0].heatIn += alHeat;
                alLeft -= 1;
            }
            else if (alPool > 1.0e-7f && house[0].t > 750.0f && shaft[0].omega < omegaMax[0])
            {
                alSeed += 1;
                if (randf(alSeed + 7919) > 0.9935f)
                {
                    const float q = alPool * 43.0e6f * 0.7f;
                    alHeat = q / (48.0f * dt);
                    alLeft = 48;
                    alPool = 0.0f;
                    alKick = q / 400.0f;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    // The charge path: flows into and out of the volumes, the volumes stepped, then the inertial flows
    void chargeSide()
    {
        // the filter: what the wheels drew from outside the sample before
        // (its loss at most half the air's pressure: a filter sized for the engine (2.5 kPa at its matched flow)
        // passes far more only past any filter's choke; unbounded, a 50 cc engine's blower put the inlet below 0 and
        // the machine diverged at the start, card X's X-026. Normal builds never come near it)
        p1 = turbos == 0 && sc == 0 ? pOut : fmaxf(pOut - kFilter * mInlet * fabsf(mInlet), 0.5f * pOut);
        // (the inlet has no volume: its pressure is the filter's loss. What flows back into it (a recirculating
        // blow-off valve, a supercharger's bypass, a sequential pair's bleed) changes that loss as it flows, by
        // 2 kFilter |m| a kg/s: those orifices are solved with it as with a volume's stiffness, and the compressors'
        // ducts likewise. Taken a sample late instead, on a small engine's filter (kFilter as 1/mMatch^2) with a big
        // compressor the loop through the valve gains: card X's X-024, an 85 mm inducer on 0.23 L, ran to megapascals
        // standing still)
        const float kIn = turbos == 0 && sc == 0 ? 0.0f : 2.0f * kFilter * fabsf(mInlet);
        const float mFresh = fmaxf(mInlet, 0.0f);
        // (what was sent back out of the inlet comes back in warm: mixed with the fresh air by their flows)
        t1 = mBack > 1.0e-6f ? (mFresh * tOut + mBack * tBack) / fmaxf(mFresh + mBack, 1.0e-6f) : tOut;
        t1 = fmaxf(t1, tOut);
        float mIn = 0.0f;
        float mOutBack = 0.0f;
        float hOutBack = 0.0f;
        for (int t = 0; t < turbos; ++t)
        {
            const float m = comp[t].mdot;
            const float pIn = compIn[t] == 1 ? vInter.p : p1;
            const float tIn = compIn[t] == 1 ? vInter.t : t1;
            comp[t].p1 = pIn;
            comp[t].t1 = tIn;
            float tOutl = 0.0f;
            if (compOut[t] == 0)
                tOutl = v1.t;
            else if (compOut[t] == 1)
                tOutl = vInter.t;
            else
                tOutl = vSec.t;
            if (compOut[t] == 0)
                v1.flow(m, comp[t].t2, 0.232f);
            else if (compOut[t] == 1)
                vInter.flow(m, comp[t].t2, 0.232f);
            else
                vSec.flow(m, comp[t].t2, 0.232f);
            if (compIn[t] == 1)
                vInter.flow(-m, tOutl, 0.232f);
            else
            {
                mIn += m;
                if (m < 0.0f)
                {
                    mOutBack -= m;
                    hOutBack -= m * tOutl;
                }
            }
        }
        if (turbos == 0 && sc == 0)
        {
            v1.flow(mNa, t1, 0.232f);
            mIn += mNa;
        }
        if (sc == 1 || sc == 2)
        {
            const float n = omegaCrank * 0.15915494f * scRatio;
            pd.step(n, p1, t1, v1.p, v1.t, boostStiff(v1.vol, v1.t, 1.4f, dt));
            v1.flow(pd.mDel, pd.t2, 0.232f);
            // (the clearances' leak runs back to the inlet; when the inlet stands above the charge pipe (cranking, a blower
            // far larger than its engine) it runs the other way, and what comes in is the inlet's air: entered at 0 K and
            // no oxygen, it cooled the charge pipe to its floor and its mass grew without its pressure answering, to
            // megapascals and non-finite while running (card X's corner seed 298, card N1))
            v1.flow(-pd.mLeak, t1, 0.232f);
            mIn += pd.mDel - pd.mLeak;
            mOutBack += pd.mLeak;
            hOutBack += pd.mLeak * v1.t;
            scDrive = pd.drive;
            sumScAir += (double)(pd.power * dt);
        }
        if (sc != 0 && scBypass != 0)
        {
            const float m = boostOrificeStep(v1.p, v1.t, p1, t1, bypassArea * bypassOpen, 0, boostStiff(v1.vol, v1.t, 1.4f, dt) + kIn);
            v1.flow(-m, t1, 0.232f);
            mIn -= m;
            if (m > 0.0f)
            {
                mOutBack += m;
                hOutBack += m * v1.t;
            }
        }
        if (layout == BOOST_SEQUENTIAL)
        {
            // the second compressor's outlet joins through its check valve as it opens; shut, a bleed keeps it from
            // dead-heading
            const float kk = boostStiff(vSec.vol, vSec.t, 1.4f, dt) + boostStiff(v1.vol, v1.t, 1.4f, dt);
            const float m = fmaxf(boostOrificeStep(vSec.p, vSec.t, v1.p, v1.t, aSecValve * seqOpen, 0, kk), 0.0f);
            vSec.flow(-m, 0.0f, 0.0f);
            v1.flow(m, vSec.t, 0.232f);
            const float mb = boostOrificeStep(vSec.p, vSec.t, p1, t1, 0.15f * comp[1].aInd * (1.0f - seqOpen), 0, boostStiff(vSec.vol, vSec.t, 1.4f, dt) + kIn);
            vSec.flow(-mb, t1, 0.232f);
            mIn -= mb;
            if (mb > 0.0f)
            {
                mOutBack += mb;
                hOutBack += mb * vSec.t;
            }
        }
        // the intercooler: the duct's flow, cooled against its core
        {
            const float m = mIc;
            const float tin = m >= 0.0f ? v1.t : v2.t;
            const float q = icEff * fabsf(m) * kBoostCpA * (tin - tCore);
            tIcOut = tin - (fabsf(m) > 1.0e-7f ? q / (fabsf(m) * kBoostCpA) : 0.0f);
            if (m >= 0.0f)
            {
                v1.flow(-m, 0.0f, 0.0f);
                v2.flow(m, tIcOut, v1.o2);
            }
            else
            {
                v2.flow(m, 0.0f, 0.0f);
                v1.flow(-m, tIcOut, v2.o2);
            }
            qCore += q * dt;
        }
        // the blow-off valve, from before the throttle: to the air, or back to the compressor's inlet
        mBov = 0.0f;
        if (bovKind != 0 && bovAt > 1.0e-6f)
        {
            const float pd2 = bovKind == 1 ? pOut : p1;
            mBov = fmaxf(boostOrificeStep(v2.p, v2.t, pd2, tOut, bovArea * bovAt, 0, boostStiff(v2.vol, v2.t, 1.4f, dt) + (bovKind == 1 ? 0.0f : kIn)), 0.0f);
            v2.flow(-mBov, 0.0f, 0.0f);
            if (bovKind == 2)
            {
                mIn -= mBov;
                mOutBack += mBov;
                hOutBack += mBov * v2.t;
            }
            sumMBov += (double)(mBov * dt);
        }
        // nitrous: into the charge before the throttle, its evaporation taking heat
        mNitrous = 0.0f;
        if (nRated > 0.0f && cmdNitrous != 0 && nLeft > 0.0f)
        {
            const float full = nLeft / fmaxf(nBottle, 0.01f);
            mNitrous = nRated * sqrtf(0.65f + 0.35f * full);
            nLeft -= mNitrous * dt;
            v2.flow(mNitrous, 288.0f, 0.364f);
            v2.heat(-mNitrous * 3.0e5f);
            sumMNitrous += (double)(mNitrous * dt);
        }
        if (purge > 0.0f && nLeft > 0.0f)
            nLeft -= 0.5f * nRated * purge * dt;
        // the intake's draw
        v2.flow(-mDraw, v2.t, v2.o2);
        sumMDraw += (double)(mDraw * dt);
        // the volumes, then the inertial flows against their new pressures
        v1.step(dt);
        v2.step(dt);
        if (layout == BOOST_COMPOUND)
            vInter.step(dt);
        if (layout == BOOST_SEQUENTIAL)
            vSec.step(dt);
        for (int t = 0; t < turbos; ++t)
        {
            float p2 = v1.p;
            if (compOut[t] == 1)
                p2 = vInter.p;
            else if (compOut[t] == 2)
                p2 = vSec.p;
            comp[t].step(p2);
        }
        {
            const float d = v1.p - v2.p;
            const float a = fabsf(mIc);
            // (and a linear part, 4 kPa a kg/s, as the compressor's duct: at rest its ring dies away)
            mIc += icDuct * (d - icK * mIc * a - 4000.0f * mIc) / (1.0f + icDuct * (2.0f * icK * a + 4000.0f));
        }
        if (turbos == 0 && sc == 0)
        {
            // (the filter's loss is the duct's own here: kFilter m |m|)
            const float a = fabsf(mNa);
            mNa += icDuct * (pOut - v1.p - kFilter * mNa * a - 4000.0f * mNa) / (1.0f + icDuct * (2.0f * kFilter * a + 4000.0f));
        }
        mInlet = mIn;
        mBack = mOutBack;
        tBack = mOutBack > 1.0e-7f ? hOutBack / mOutBack : tOut;
        for (int t = 0; t < turbos; ++t)
            if (compIn[t] == 0)
                sumMComp += (double)(comp[t].mdot * dt);
        if (sc == 1 || sc == 2)
            sumMComp += (double)((pd.mDel - pd.mLeak) * dt);
    }

    void sounds()
    {
        float rushLevel = 0.0f;
        float whistle = 0.0f;
        for (int t = 0; t < turbos; ++t)
        {
            const float sh = fminf(shaft[t].omega / omegaMax[t], 1.2f);
            const float flowShare = fminf(fabsf(comp[t].mdot) / fmaxf(comp[t].mc, 1.0e-4f), 1.0f);
            rushLevel += sh * sh * flowShare;
            if (sc == 0)
                whistle += snd.whistle(t, sh * sh);
        }
        const float rho = pOut / (kBoostR * tOut);
        const float bovRef = fmaxf(bovArea * 450.0f, 1.0e-4f);
        const float bv = fminf(mBov / bovRef, 1.5f);
        const float bovAir = bovKind == 1 ? bv * bv : 0.0f;
        const float bovRe = bovKind == 2 ? bv * bv : 0.0f;
        snd.tick(mInlet / rho, rushLevel / sqrtf((float)(turbos > 0 ? turbos : 1)), bovAir, bovRe, purge, alKick);
        outInlet = snd.inlet + whistle / sqrtf((float)(turbos > 0 ? turbos : 1));
        outVent = snd.vent;
        outBang = snd.bang;
        outCase = 0.0f;
        if (sc != 0)
        {
            // a positive-displacement blower's pockets (six a turn of a Roots's rotors, four of a twin-screw's male
            // rotor); a centrifugal's gear mesh (31 teeth on its input gear)
            const float n = omegaCrank * 0.15915494f * scRatio;
            const float pockets = sc == 1 ? 6.0f : (sc == 2 ? 4.0f : 31.0f);
            const float sp = fminf(omegaCrank / 600.0f, 1.0f);
            const float ld = fminf(fmaxf((v1.p - pOut) / 80000.0f, 0.0f), 1.0f);
            outCase = snd.whine(pockets * n, n, sp * (0.3f + 0.7f * ld));
        }
    }

    // Card C's settle (spec.boost.heatSettle): the intercooler's core put where the present flow and the air through
    // it hold it (its steady state: the charge's heat, effectiveness times the flow times the temperature over the
    // core's, equal to the cooling air's, gCool times the core over the air), as G's exhaust and C's intake settle
    // their walls: a dyno's sweep without waiting the core's 15 to 25 s
    void settleCore()
    {
        const float h = icEff * mIcSlow * kBoostCpA;
        tCore = (h * tIcInSlow + gCool * tOut) / fmaxf(h + gCool, 1.0e-3f);
        if (cellHeld != 0)
            tCore = tOut;
    }

    // ---- every 16 samples -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    void control(float d16) [[clang::nonblocking]]
    {
        if (active == 0)
            return;
        const float boost = v2.p - pOut;
        const float signal = v1.p - pOut;
        const float tg = cmdTarget >= 0.0f ? cmdTarget : target;
        // the loop: the boost before the throttle to its target
        float u = 0.0f;
        if (tg > 0.0f)
        {
            const float e = (tg - boost) / tg;
            integ = fminf(fmaxf(integ + 4.0f * e * d16, -0.5f), 1.0f);
            u = fminf(fmaxf(2.5f * e + integ, 0.0f), 0.95f);
        }
        else
            integ = 0.0f;
        duty = u;
        // electric assist: below the target (or the spring, the pedal down), the motor helps
        const float want = tg > 0.0f ? tg : gateSpring;
        assistCmd = pPlenum > 0.85f * pOut ? fminf(fmaxf(3.0f * (want - boost) / want, 0.0f), 1.0f) : 0.0f;
        flags = 0;
        for (int t = 0; t < turbos; ++t)
        {
            // the map at the shaft's speed
            float pIn = p1;
            float tIn = t1;
            if (compIn[t] == 1)
            {
                pIn = vInter.p;
                tIn = vInter.t;
            }
            comp[t].speed(shaft[t].omega, pIn, tIn);
            if (sc == 3)
                continue;
            // the gate: its spring against the boost's signal (bled by the duty) and the exhaust's push on its poppet
            const int hh = 2 * t;
            const float push = kFace * (house[hh].p - pOut);
            float s = signal * (1.0f - (turb[t].vgt != 0 ? 0.0f : duty)) + push;
            if (layout == BOOST_SEQUENTIAL && t == 1)
                s = signal + push;
            const float open = fminf(fmaxf((s - gateSpring) / gateSpan, 0.0f), 1.0f);
            turb[t].lift += (open - turb[t].lift) * (1.0f - expf(-d16 / 0.04f));
            if (turb[t].vgt != 0)
            {
                float v = 0.0f;
                if (cmdVanes >= 0.0f)
                    v = cmdVanes;
                else if (tg > 0.0f)
                    v = 1.0f - u;
                else
                    v = turb[t].vaneMin + (1.0f - turb[t].vaneMin) * fminf(fmaxf((signal - 0.8f * gateSpring) / (0.2f * gateSpring + gateSpan), 0.0f), 1.0f);
                // (the exhaust's back-pressure limit, as a production VGT controller's: past bpLimit times the boost,
                // absolute, the vanes are opened by an integral of the excess whatever the boost loop asks, for shut
                // vanes against a compressor that cannot deliver only pump the engine (the 15 L tractor lost a third of
                // its torque so, PMEP 2.5 to 5 bar). The 1.4 default is judgement: makers hold some 1.2 to 1.5 at rated
                // power; a maker's calibration would replace it. Not while the ECU commands the vanes (an engine brake))
                if (cmdVanes < 0.0f)
                {
                    const float r3 = house[hh].p / fmaxf(v2.p, 1000.0f);
                    bpOpen[t] = fminf(fmaxf(bpOpen[t] + d16 * 3.0f * (r3 - bpLimit), 0.0f), 1.0f);
                    v = fmaxf(v, turb[t].vaneMin + bpOpen[t]);
                    // (the surge guard, gain-reversal protection: vanes shut past the compressor's surge line make
                    // less boost, not more: it cannot deliver, the engine's air and the diesel's smoke-limited fuel fall
                    // and the turbine's energy with them, a second steady state below the first: card D2's 15 L truck
                    // at 1300 rpm stood at 98 kPa and 882 N m with its vanes at 0.47, surging two thirds of the time,
                    // against 209 kPa and 1945 N m at 0.9. While the compressor surges, an integral opens the vanes at
                    // 1 a second and gives back 0.3 of that rate while it does not: the vanes settle where it surges
                    // some 23 % of the time, the surge line's edge (2 a second put the 15 L tractor at 1000 rpm off its
                    // boost, 0.5 left the truck's spool a second behind a fixed nozzle's). Judgement, as the limit
                    // above is: a maker's vane map keeps its own margin)
                    const float phiS = comp[t].mdot / fmaxf(comp[t].mc, 1.0e-5f);
                    // (only the loop's own surge counts: with the pedal down (the plenum not under the throttle's
                    // vacuum, as the assist's test) and the boost short of what is asked; a lift's surge on a closed
                    // throttle is the blow-off valve's matter, and then the guard only gives back)
                    const int surging = (comp[t].mdot < 0.0f || (phiS < 0.8f * comp[t].phiK && comp[t].pr > 1.15f)) &&
                                                pPlenum > 0.85f * pOut && boost < want
                                            ? 1
                                            : 0;
                    surgeOpen[t] = fminf(fmaxf(surgeOpen[t] + d16 * 1.0f * (surging != 0 ? 1.0f : -0.3f), 0.0f), 1.0f);
                    v = fmaxf(v, turb[t].vaneMin + surgeOpen[t]);
                }
                else
                {
                    bpOpen[t] = 0.0f;
                    surgeOpen[t] = 0.0f;
                }
                v = fminf(fmaxf(v, turb[t].vaneMin), 1.0f);
                turb[t].vanes += (v - turb[t].vanes) * (1.0f - expf(-d16 / 0.05f));
                // (with vanes the gate is a relief only: well above the target)
                if (tg > 0.0f && boost < 1.2f * tg)
                    turb[t].lift = 0.0f;
            }
            // the ECU's vanes (an exhaust brake on the turbine, card D2's): it owns the turbine, so a variable nozzle's
            // gate is held shut, and the vanes stand where it puts them (0: their shut stop, vaneMin), the shaft's
            // over-speed relief below still acting
            if (turb[t].vgt != 0 && cmdVanes >= 0.0f)
                turb[t].lift = 0.0f;
            // over-speed relief, as an ECU's: past 105 % of the shaft's limit the gate and the vanes open wide
            if (shaft[t].omega > 1.05f * omegaMax[t])
            {
                turb[t].lift = 1.0f;
                turb[t].vanes = 1.0f;
            }
            // flags
            const float phi = comp[t].mdot / fmaxf(comp[t].mc, 1.0e-5f);
            if (comp[t].mdot < 0.0f || (phi < 0.8f * comp[t].phiK && comp[t].pr > 1.15f))
                flags |= BOOST_FLAG_SURGE;
            if (phi > 0.98f && comp[t].u > 50.0f)
                flags |= BOOST_FLAG_CHOKE;
            if (shaft[t].omega > omegaMax[t])
                flags |= BOOST_FLAG_OVERSPEED;
        }
        if (boost > overBoost && overBoost > 0.0f)
            flags |= BOOST_FLAG_OVERBOOST;
        // the blow-off valve: the pressure across the throttle against its spring
        {
            const float across = v2.p - pPlenum;
            const float open = bovKind != 0 ? fminf(fmaxf((across - bovSpring) / 10000.0f, 0.0f), 1.0f) : 0.0f;
            bovLift += (open - bovLift) * (1.0f - expf(-d16 / 0.003f));
            if (bovLift > 0.1f)
                flags |= BOOST_FLAG_BLOWOFF;
        }
        // sequential: the second joins above a flow
        drawMean += (mDraw - drawMean) * (1.0f - expf(-d16 / 0.1f));
        if (layout == BOOST_SEQUENTIAL)
        {
            if (drawMean > seqFlow)
                seqWant = 1.0f;
            else if (drawMean < 0.8f * seqFlow)
                seqWant = 0.0f;
            seqOpen += (seqWant - seqOpen) * (1.0f - expf(-d16 / 0.15f));
        }
        // a supercharger's bypass: open with the vacuum after the throttle
        {
            const float want2 = fminf(fmaxf((pOut - pPlenum - 5000.0f) / 25000.0f, 0.0f), 1.0f);
            bypassOpen += (want2 - bypassOpen) * (1.0f - expf(-d16 / 0.05f));
        }
        crankTorque = driveSum / 16.0f / fmaxf(omegaCrank, 10.0f);
        driveSum = 0.0f;
        // the intercooler's core: what the charge gave it, less what the air through it took. In an engine test cell
        // (MODE_DYNO_ENGINE, Boost::testCell) the core is held at the air's temperature: SAE J1349 has the laboratory's
        // charge-air cooling set so the manifold air is what the installed cooler gives at its rated condition, and
        // the cooler's own effectiveness (spec.boost.icEffect) is stated against its cooling air, so a core at the
        // air's temperature gives exactly that effectiveness. On the chassis dyno and the road, the air through the
        // car's front (the roller's or the car's speed); standing, still air
        gCool = 200.0f + 30.0f * airSpeed;
        {
            const float tin = mIc >= 0.0f ? v1.t : v2.t;
            const float kS = 1.0f - expf(-d16 / 1.0f);
            mIcSlow += (fabsf(mIc) - mIcSlow) * kS;
            tIcInSlow += (tin - tIcInSlow) * kS;
        }
        if (cellHeld != 0)
            tCore = tOut;
        else
            tCore += (qCore - d16 * gCool * (tCore - tOut)) / fmaxf(cCore, 1.0f);
        qCore = 0.0f;
        // nitrous: its purge
        if (cmdPurge != purgeSeen)
        {
            purgeSeen = cmdPurge;
            purge = 1.0f;
        }
        purge *= expf(-d16 / 0.4f);
        if (purge < 0.001f)
            purge = 0.0f;
        if (mNitrous > 0.0f)
            flags |= BOOST_FLAG_NITROUS;
        // the sounds' bands and pitches
        for (int t = 0; t < turbos; ++t)
            snd.whRot(t, shaft[t].omega * 0.15915494f);
        {
            const float sh = turbos > 0 ? fminf(shaft[0].omega / omegaMax[0], 1.2f) : 0.0f;
            const float n = omegaCrank * 0.15915494f * scRatio;
            const float pockets = sc == 1 ? 6.0f : (sc == 2 ? 4.0f : 31.0f);
            snd.control(sh, pockets * n, pd.pulse);
        }
        telemetry();
        trailTick += 1;
        if (trailTick >= 32)
        {
            trailTick = 0;
            trailFlow[trailAt] = telFlow[0];
            trailPr[trailAt] = telPr[0];
            trailAt = trailAt + 1 >= BOOST_TRAIL ? 0 : trailAt + 1;
        }
    }

    void telemetry()
    {
        for (int t = 0; t < BOOST_TURBOS; ++t)
        {
            if (t >= turbos)
            {
                telSpeed[t] = 0.0f;
                telPr[t] = 1.0f;
                telFlow[t] = 0.0f;
                telEta[t] = 0.0f;
                telT2[t] = tOut;
                telGate[t] = 0.0f;
                telVanes[t] = 1.0f;
                telPTurb[t] = pOut;
                telTTurb[t] = tOut;
                telDrive[t] = 1.0f;
                continue;
            }
            telSpeed[t] = shaft[t].omega;
            telPr[t] = comp[t].pr;
            telFlow[t] = comp[t].mdot * sqrtf(comp[t].t1 / 293.15f) / (comp[t].p1 / 101325.0f);
            telEta[t] = comp[t].eta;
            telT2[t] = comp[t].t2;
            telGate[t] = turb[t].lift;
            telVanes[t] = turb[t].vgt != 0 ? turb[t].vanes : 1.0f;
            const int h = 2 * t;
            const float ph = scrolls == 2 ? 0.5f * (house[h].p + house[h + 1].p) : house[h].p;
            telPTurb[t] = ph;
            telTTurb[t] = scrolls == 2 ? 0.5f * (house[h].t + house[h + 1].t) : house[h].t;
            telDrive[t] = ph / v1.p;
        }
        telBoost = v2.p - pOut;
        telIcOut = tIcOut;
        telScPower = sc != 0 ? crankTorque * omegaCrank : 0.0f;
        telO2 = v2.o2;
    }

    // The map's lines for a view, at the standard inlet (101325 Pa, 293.15 K): speed lines from tip Mach 0.4 to
    // 1.45, each from its knee (the surge line) to choke; efficiency contours where each line crosses a level. Off the
    // audio thread (in apply).
    void mapLines()
    {
        mapRev += 1;
        BoostCompressor c = comp[0];
        const float a0 = sqrtf(1.4f * kBoostR * 293.15f);
        for (int l = 0; l < BOOST_LINES; ++l)
        {
            const float mach = 0.4f + 0.15f * (float)l;
            const float w = mach * a0 / fmaxf(c.rTip, 1.0e-4f);
            c.speed(w, 101325.0f, 293.15f);
            lineSpeed[l] = w;
            for (int i = 0; i < BOOST_LINEPTS; ++i)
            {
                const float phi = c.phiK + (1.0f - c.phiK) * (float)i / (float)(BOOST_LINEPTS - 1);
                const float tau = c.rise(phi);
                const float cc = 1.0f + tau;
                lineFlow[l][i] = phi * c.mc;
                linePr[l][i] = cc * cc * cc * sqrtf(cc);
            }
            surgeFlow[l] = lineFlow[l][0];
            surgePr[l] = linePr[l][0];
            for (int v = 0; v < BOOST_LEVELS; ++v)
            {
                const float levels[BOOST_LEVELS] = {0.02f, 0.05f, 0.08f, 0.12f, 0.18f};
                const float level = c.etaMax - levels[v];
                contourEta[v] = level;
                const float room = c.etaM - level;
                float fl = -1.0f;
                float fr = -1.0f;
                float pl = 1.0f;
                float pr = 1.0f;
                if (room > 0.0f)
                {
                    const float dphi = sqrtf(room / 0.9f);
                    const float phl = c.phiB - dphi;
                    const float phr = c.phiB + dphi;
                    if (phl > 0.0f)
                    {
                        const float cl = 1.0f + c.rise(phl);
                        fl = phl * c.mc;
                        pl = cl * cl * cl * sqrtf(cl);
                    }
                    if (phr < 1.0f)
                    {
                        const float cr = 1.0f + c.rise(phr);
                        fr = phr * c.mc;
                        pr = cr * cr * cr * sqrtf(cr);
                    }
                }
                contourFlow[v][l] = fl;
                contourPr[v][l] = pl;
                contourFlow[v][BOOST_CONTOUR - 1 - l] = fr;
                contourPr[v][BOOST_CONTOUR - 1 - l] = pr;
            }
        }
    }
};
